DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sin((cos(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("sin((e^((x^3))))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-5, 10} U ({-5, 10}) U {-3, -2, 10}");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-5, 10} U {-5, 10} U {-5, 10} U {-3, -2, 10}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-3, -2, 10} U {-5, 10}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(-infinity, 16] U (9, infinity) U (-infinity, 16] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-2, 1, 3, 5, 6, 8}) U ((-infinity, 16] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-2, 1, 3, 5, 6, 8}))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-2, 1, 3, 5, 6, 8} U (-infinity, 16] U (9, infinity)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`0+11-2`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(9.),width=>3}
---

What is the value of [`4*15+10*2`]? [_____]{80}
---

What is the value of [`18+9+10-17*19`]? [_____]{Real(-286.)}
---

[`7+11-2+16*8`] is equal to [_____]{144}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-2, 1, 3, 5, 6, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 8\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 16\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup B \cup C \cap A \cup (C \cap A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-3, -2, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup (B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup B \cup B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, 4, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -10, -10, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -6, -1, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, 4, 10>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -1, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-7, 4, 10>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 4, 10>") . Compute("<-10, -10, 2>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, -1, 5>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -1, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, 2, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, -6, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, 2, -2>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, -6, 7>") . Compute("<-7, 2, -2>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -6, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-7, 2, -2>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 2, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 2, -2>") . Compute("<2, -6, 7>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>0)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
